<p class="lede">Bayan 0.4.1 is the current release, a prerelease. It builds on 0.4.0, where the compiler became a Bayan program needing only a C compiler. This page covers both; the full list is in the <a href="https://github.com/ikhbat-org/bayan/blob/v0.4.1/CHANGELOG.md">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>

<h2 id="self-hosted">A compiler written in Bayan</h2>
<p>The compiler, test runner and language server are Bayan programs. The repository keeps it as one C file, <code>bootstrap/bayan.c</code>, so any C11 compiler builds it; <a href="install.html#build">Install Bayan</a> has the command.</p>

<h2 id="lsp">The language server ships with the compiler</h2>
<p>Every release archive holds <code>bayan-lsp</code> (<code>bayan-lsp.exe</code> on Windows) beside <code>bayan</code>. Point your editor's language client at it; <a href="https://github.com/ikhbat-org/bayan/blob/v0.4.1/editors/README.md">editors/README.md</a> describes the VS Code extension.</p>

<h2 id="test">bayan test runs golden cases</h2>
<p><code>bayan test tests/cases</code> runs the compiler's golden cases itself, programs beside their required output, and prints one line per failure with its first differing line.</p>

<h2 id="std">New in the standard library</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Area</th><th>API</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>std.regex</code></td><td><code>Regex.parse</code>, then <code>matches</code>, <code>find</code>, <code>findAll</code>, <code>replaced(text, by:)</code> and <code>Regex.escaped</code></td><td>matching takes time linear in the length of the text</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>std.encoding</code></td><td><code>Base64.encode</code> and <code>Base64.decode</code></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>Glob patterns</td><td><code>Glob.matches(pattern, for: path)</code> in <code>std.path</code>, and <code>glob(pattern)</code> in <code>std.fs</code></td><td><code>glob</code> lists the files a pattern names</td></tr>
</table>
